Provers
-------

Vampire 5.0.1, the release binary (commit 1b13eaf), one problem at a time:
version 1 with --mode casc at 60 s; version 2 with --mode casc at 300 s
and, for a Satisfiable problem casc did not solve, --mode casc_sat at
300 s. The repository also decides every pair with Z3 4.8.12 on an SMT-LIB
encoding of the same statements; that encoding is not part of this export.

Version 1: 122 of 122 solved with the stated status. Version 2: 92 solved
with --mode casc; 0 not solved within the limit.

The slowest version 2 problems:

    KGC099+2   KGC388-1   Satisfiable     casc         42.0 s
    KGC098+2   KGC383-2   Unsatisfiable   casc          6.0 s
    KGC093+2   KGC380-1   Satisfiable     casc          1.7 s
    KGC101+2   KGC391-1   Satisfiable     casc          1.6 s
    KGC097+2   KGC383-1   Satisfiable     casc          1.6 s
    KGC095+2   KGC382-1   Satisfiable     casc          1.6 s
    KGC041+2   KGC333-1   Satisfiable     casc          1.6 s
    KGC039+2   KGC331-1   Satisfiable     casc          1.6 s
    KGC094+2   KGC380-2   Unsatisfiable   casc          1.0 s
    KGC042+2   KGC333-2   Satisfiable     casc          0.5 s

Every file parses with tptp4X -x -w, includes expanded, with no warning.
tptp4X was built from the TPTP World sources (github.com/TPTPWorld/TPTP4X
at ce83fd4, JJParser at 94a781a).

Layout
------

    Problems/KGC/KGCnnn+1.p    version 1
    Problems/KGC/KGCnnn+2.p    version 2
    Axioms/KGC000+0.ax         the order axioms
    Axioms/KGC000+1.ax ...     one file per vocabulary
    manifest.csv               one row per problem: problem, version,
                               original name, case, check, status,
                               case verdict, axiom files, Vampire
                               result, mode, time

Includes are written include('Axioms/KGC000+N.ax'), relative to this
folder.

